TECHNICAL SPECIFICATION: REST API BACKEND AND DATA STRUCTURE OF THE VEO360 DIGITAL TWIN PLATFORM
1. System architecture and general principles
1.1 Introductory context and strategic significance
A backend service based on the high-performance FastAPI framework serves as the central architectural core of the VEO360 digital twin platform. The server-side component ensures strict decoupling between the autonomous offline computer vision pipeline (which extracts data from ASTM E57 spatial scans, performs hardware detection, and optical character recognition (OCR)) and external client visualization interfaces (3D Viewer / Matterport). Interacting via a standardized REST API, the backend aggregates attribute and spatial data, manages the digital twin's topological graph, indexes regulatory and technical documentation, and provides deterministic data contracts for client web applications.
1.2 Data flow analysis and separation of concerns
The transfer of spatial and attribute data in the VEO360 platform is organized as a consistent end-to-end pipeline:
\text{Panorama frames (skybox)} \longrightarrow \text{Offline model (detect + OCR)} \longrightarrow \texttt{detections.json} \longrightarrow \texttt{POST /detections} \longrightarrow \text{Tags/devices database} \longrightarrow \texttt{GET /tags} \longrightarrow \text{3D Viewer}
The system architecture clearly delineates areas of responsibility: the FastAPI backendisolated from performing direct heavy calculationsover multi-gigabyte E57 point clouds and panoramic frames. All resource-intensive geometric back-projection (raycasting) and scan processing operations are performed exclusively within the autonomous offline pipeline (process_e57.py / e57/raycast.py). The FastAPI HTTP service receives through an endpointPOST /detectionsa ready-made structured JSON dump of detections containing pre-calculated 3D world coordinates (x, y, z) or raw 2D bounding boxes. If the detection is received without 3D coordinates (position == null), the backend does not try to run spatial calculations on the fly, but keeps the device in the unallocated status (unassigned) with the required check flag set (needs_review = true).
The key software modules of the backend and autonomous pipeline are:
backend/main.py: The main FastAPI executable module, which contains web application initialization, HTTP request routing, Pydantic schema declaration, processing of business logic for binding devices to cabinets, and primary seed initialization of the database.
backend/storage.py: File Storage Abstraction Module (LocalStorage), implementing the persistence interfaces (save), existence checks (exists), formation of URLs (url) and file search (find). Using the "Strategy" pattern allows for seamless migration of the local file system to S3-compatible cloud storage (AWS S3, Azure Blob Storage) without making changes to the routers.backend/main.py.
e57/raycast.py: Isolated offline spatial geometry module (called withinprocess_e57.py), which performs matching of 2D coordinates of pixels in skybox frames with 3D point cloud E57 using the ray intersection method with the front surface of the object.
knowledge/adapter.py: A knowledge base integration module that wraps the full-text search algorithm (scripts/kb_search.py) for semantic matching of detected equipment classes with operating manuals.
