Parameter estimationCONF_MIN And MAX_ASSIGN_DISTdemonstrates their critical influence on the correctness of the formation of the equipment topological graph:
Overstating the thresholdCONF_MINleads to the fact that highly accurate detections with minor deviations in confidence are massively flaggedneeds_review = true, generating false tasks for the operator. UnderestimationCONF_MINentails the automatic addition of false-positive computer vision artifacts into the working contour of the digital twin without verification.
UnderstatementMAX_ASSIGN_DISTleads to a break in communication: correctly detected protection relays remain in the unattached status (unassigned), even if they are physically mounted on the front panel of the cabinet. OverestimationMAX_ASSIGN_DISTIn conditions of dense arrangement of distribution device (RU) cells, this leads to an erroneous connection of the device to the adjacent cabinet, distorting the actual topology of the electrical network.
The resulting separation of system responsibilities and configuration model provide a platform for designing a relational data storage structure.
2. Structure and schema of relational databases
2.1 Introductory context and strategic significance
To ensure a balance between the speed of web query processing, the detail of spatial analysis and the efficiency of full-text search, the VEO360 platform implements a hybrid division of data into three specialized SQLite databases: an operational relational entity database (data/veo.db), knowledge base of technical documentation (data/knowledge.db) and an extended spatial localization database (dataset/veo_localization.db).
2.2 Database diagram of operational tags and devices (data/veo.db)
Operational databasedata/veo.dbDesigned to handle low-latency requests from the REST API, the backend automatically initializes the table structure and performs an initial seed load of 10 reference cell cabinets upon first launch:H05, H04, H03, H02, H01, WOLF, OT1, TSK1, TSK2, OKK1.
An important architectural feature: during initializationdata/veo.dbspatial coordinates (x, and, With), confidence indicators (confidence), context images and device lists for cabinets are seeded with valuesnull/ empty arrays. Full filling of the attribute composition occurs exogenously - either by calling batch importPOST /import/cabinets, or when processing incoming detectionsPOST /detections.
The essence of a cabinet (tag) includes the following attribute composition:
id (str): Unique identifier of the cabinet (eg."H05").
name (str): The display name of the cell.
folder (str): Hierarchical folder/equipment group (default)"Switchgear").
position (Position3D): Coordinates of the centroid{x, y, z}in the world coordinate system of the scan.
confidence (float): Aggregated indicator of position determination confidence.
needs_review (bool): Flag indicating the need for manual audit by the operator.
image (str): Relative URL path to the cabinet context image.
image_is_placeholder (bool): A sign that a default placeholder is being used instead of a real photo.
read_as (str): The marking text read by the OCR module.
sightings (int): The total number of angles/scans at which the object is captured.
evidence_crop (str): Path to the cut frame-proof of detection.
doc_models (list[str]): List of equipment models for the official connection with documentation.
documents (list[DocumentOut]): An array of strictly validated objects of linked documents.
devices (list[DeviceOut]): List of devices mounted on the cabinet (e.g. relaysabb_relion_615).
Strong data typing at the FastAPI and OpenAPI specification level is provided by deterministic Pydantic models:
