2.3 Knowledge base and full-text search scheme (data/knowledge.db)
The knowledge base stores the structured content of technical operating manuals. The schema consists of two basic tables and one virtual FTS5 table:
Tabledocuments:
id (INTEGER PRIMARY KEY): Unique numeric identifier of the document.
title (TEXT): The full title of the manual (e.g."ABB 615 Protection Relay Manual").
model (TEXT): Equipment model ("ABB 615", "UniGear ZS2", "VD4").
doc_number (TEXT): Document nomenclature number (e.g."1MRS756500").
pdf_path (TEXT): Path to the original PDF file relative toDOCS_DIR.
pages (INTEGER): Document volume in pages.
Tablechunks:
id (INTEGER PRIMARY KEY): Text fragment identifier.
doc_id (INTEGER FOREIGN KEY): Link to documents(id).
section_path (TEXT): Hierarchical path to the section (e.g."3. Protection Functions / 3.2 READY LED Status").
page_start (INTEGER): Initial page of the fragment.
page_end (INTEGER): The final page of the fragment.
text (TEXT): Extracted text content with explicit page breaks<!-- p.N -->.
FTS5 Virtual Tablechunks_fts:
Initialized via the SQLite FTS5 module: CREATE VIRTUAL TABLE chunks_fts USING fts5(text, content='chunks', content_rowid='id').
Performance analysis shows that despite the time required for the initial index build (about 5 minutes for the 1,985-page REX615 manual,scripts/ingest_docs.py), FTS5 provides instant (less than 15 milliseconds) full-text search with model limitationd.model = 'ABB 615', returning exact text fragments and page ranges.
