4. Algorithms for 2D/3D localization and detection processing
4.1 Introductory context and strategic significance
Correct translation of two-dimensional bounding boxes[x, y, w, h]The conversion of the panoramic frame's pixel grid into the scan's 3D world coordinates (X, Y, Z) is key to the physical accuracy of the digital twin. This calculation is performed in the offline pipeline (process_e57.py) using the geometric modulee57/raycast.py.
4.2 Raycasting / Point Cloud Intersection Algorithm
The back projection and intersection point search algorithm consists of five deterministic steps:
Loading a local point cloud: Stream reading of array of XYZ coordinates of a specific scanner stop is performed viae57.read_scan(i)without fully loading the E57 file into RAM.
Transition to the camera coordinate system (Extrinsics): The world coordinates of the scan points P_{\text{world}} = (X, Y, Z)^T are transformed into the camera coordinate system P_c = (X_c, Y_c, Z_c)^T using the camera center translation vector C and the camera-to-world rotation matrix R_{c2w}:
P_c = R_{c2w}^T (P_{\text{world}} - C)
Pinhole projection onto a pixel grid (Intrinsics): The points P_c are projected into 2D frame pixels (u, v) using the focal length f and the optical center (c_x, c_y):
\begin{pmatrix} u \\ v \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} f \cdot \frac{X_c}{Z_c} + c_x \\ f \cdot \frac{Y_c}{Z_c} + c_y \end{pmatrix}
Filtering by 2D Bounding Box and Front Plane Selection:
3D points whose pixel coordinates (u, v) fall inside the detection rectangle are selectednear: \text{near} = (u, v) \in [\text{box}_{xmin}, \text{box}_{xmax}] \times [\text{box}_{ymin}, \text{box}_{ymax}]
To prevent the beam from shooting through transparent or open elements, the background is cut off and the front physical surface is selected by depth z: \text{front} = z < \left( z_{min} \cdot 1.05 + 0.03 \right)
3D anchor calculation: The final anchor coordinates are calculated as the median of the filtered front surface coordinates: \text{Anchor}_{3D} = \text{median}(\text{xyz}[\text{near}][\text{front}], \text{axis}=0)
Approximation of focal length: If the parameterpinholeRepresentation.focalLengthis missing from the E57 metadata, the system automatically approximates the focal length as half the frame width (f = W / 2).
4.3 Logic of automatic device binding and verification criteria (needs_review)
After receiving the 3D coordinates of the device, the FastAPI backend is calledPOST /detectionsperforms its automatic binding to the spatial graph:
The Euclidean distance from P_{\text{device}}(x,y,z) to the centroids of all registered cabinets is calculated.
If the minimum distance d_{min} \le \text{MAX\_ASSIGN\_DIST} (default 2.0 m), the device automatically communicates with the cabinet (cabinet_id = cabinet.id).
If d_{min} > \text{MAX\_ASSIGN\_DIST}, the device is stored with the valuecabinet_id = null.
The detection is automatically flagged.needs_review = truewith adding records to the arrayreview_reasonsif any of the conditions are met:
Classification confidence is below the established threshold:conf < CONF_MIN.
Missing 3D coordinates:position == null(the model only transferred 2D bbox).
Auto-binding threshold exceeded: d_{min} > \text{MAX\_ASSIGN\_DIST} (the nearest cabinet is too far away).
The generated spatial graph is transferred to the knowledge base integration subsystem for linking documentation.
5. Knowledge base integration and documentation linking
5.1 Introductory context and strategic significance
Automatically linking technical manuals to digital twin objects reduces labor costs for servicing reactor cells, speeds up the search for emergency response procedures, and provides instant access to operating documentation.
5.2 Mapping equipment classes to technical documentation
The comparison of recognized device classes with technical documentation models is carried out through a dictionaryDEVICE_CLASSES V backend/main.py:
DEVICE_CLASSES = {
    "abb_relion_615": ("ABB 615 protection relay", "ABB 615"),
    "relay_front": ("ABB 615 protection relay", "ABB 615"),
    "relay_rear": ("ABB 615 protection relay", "ABB 615")
}

All three detection class keys (abb_relion_615, relay_front, relay_rear) are clearly translated into a single target management model"ABB 615".
Cabinets (tags) are linked to technical documentation via an attributedoc_models:
Closet H05has pre-installed static links to manual models"UniGear ZS2" And "VD4".
All other cabinets (H04–H01, WOLF, OT1, TSK1, TSK2, OKK1) have empty documentation lists when initialized and are linked to books either upon receipt of detections or manually via an HTTP requestPATCH /tags/{id}by passing a list of models in the fielddoc_models.
5.3 Search and citation mechanism in/ask
The RAG/FTS search mechanism implemented inknowledge/adapter.py(based onscripts/kb_search.py), is executed according to the following algorithm:
When callingPOST /askan SQL query is generated for the virtual FTS5 tablechunks_ftsknowledge basesdata/knowledge.db.
Filtering is performed by the equipment model field (d.model = 'ABB 615').
From the tablechunksRelevant text fragments, document titles, and the hierarchical path to the section are extracted (section_path) and page range (page_start, page_end).
An array of passages is generated with direct URL links to a PDF file with a page navigation anchor (/documents/{doc_id}/file#page={page_start}).
